%I A401976 #8 Nov 12 2026 09:32:07
%S A401976 1,5,4,9,6,7,5,2,5,7,0,0,3,9,3,1,4,1,6,1,8,8,1,8,9,7,0,5,9,5,4,5,7,4,
%T A401976 4,0,6,9,3,8,7,5,7,5,0,3,0,7,6,0,1,6,8,0,7,0,7,3,8,0,3,1,5,4,5,1,9,8,
%U A401976 6,7,1,1,0,8,6,9,5,7,9,7,9,9,1,7,0,5,3
%N A401976 Decimal expansion of (4/3)*(L(2) + L'(2)) + L'(1/2)/24, where L(s) = xi'(s)/xi(s) and xi is the Riemann xi function.
%C A401976 This is h_0 = u_0, the zeroth term of the cubic Chebyshev trace u_n = Sum_rho theta_rho*T_n(1 - 2*theta_rho), with theta_rho = -27/(4*q(rho)^2), q(s) = (s-2)*(s+1)*(2*s-1)/(2*s*(s-1)), and rho running over the nontrivial zeros of zeta. The formula in the name comes from residues of xi'/xi at s = -1, 1/2, 2, so no zeros are needed to compute it.
%C A401976 Rouyea and Bourgeois prove that the Riemann hypothesis is equivalent to |u_n| <= h_0 for all n >= 0.
%H A401976 Blaize Rouyea and Corey Bourgeois, <a href="https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2610.zeroth-chebyshev-trace-local-formula">A Local Formula for the Zeroth Chebyshev Trace</a>, alphaXiv preprint (2026).
%H A401976 Blaize Rouyea and Corey Bourgeois, <a href="https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2608.chebyshev-trace-riemann-hypothesis">A Chebyshev Trace Criterion for the Riemann Hypothesis</a>, alphaXiv preprint (2026).
%F A401976 If the Riemann hypothesis is true, this equals Sum_{k>=1} tanh(3*arctanh(sqrt(3)/(2*g_k)))^2, where g_k is the imaginary part of the k-th nontrivial zero of zeta. Numerically, the first 400 zeros give 0.14599320674998953..., leaving a tail of about 0.0089743.
%e A401976 0.15496752570039314161881897059545744069387575030760168070738...
%t A401976 RealDigits[-2*EulerGamma/3 + Pi^2/18 - 48*Zeta'[2]^2/Pi^4 + (8*Catalan + Pi^2 - 64*Log[Pi] - (EulerGamma + Pi/2 + Log[8*Pi])^2 + (4*Zeta''[1/2])/Zeta[1/2])/96 + 8*(Zeta'[2] + Zeta''[2])/Pi^2, 10, 105][[1]] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 11 2026 *)
%o A401976 (Python)
%o A401976 from mpmath import mp, mpf, zeta, gamma, log, pi, diff
%o A401976 mp.dps = 120
%o A401976 lx = lambda s: log(s/2*(s-1)) - s/2*log(pi) + log(gamma(s/2)) + log(zeta(s))
%o A401976 print(mp.nstr((mpf(4)/3*(diff(lx, 2) + diff(lx, 2, 2)) + diff(lx, mpf(1)/2, 2)/24).real, 90))
%Y A401976 Cf. A332645.
%K A401976 nonn,cons,new
%O A401976 0,2
%A A401976 _Blaize Rouyea_, Nov 10 2026
